!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/valid/how-a-record-may-be-realised-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2"
  description: "How a record may be realised is a fact of the resolved body and not an annotation: the marks are consumed and `record.extension` carries what they said, so a resolver that preserved them instead would show them in the annotation channel and leave every record OPEN. Each of the three members appears once here. **How a record may be realised and how its members are selected are two facts**: `pet` and `shape` are both ABSTRACT, and what makes `pet` dispatch on its members rather than on the tag is the non-empty `record.discriminators` beside it. A base names those fields in the order their pins are compared as a tuple: which fields select is the base's own statement about its family, not a property of each field in isolation. A member inherits the base's fields by §5.8 flattening and states no discriminators of its own, so it restates the selector to pin the value and never to claim a family. OPEN and false are the defaults and are omitted, as every default is."
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  valid: {
    resolved: """
      !schema {
        pet => !type_definition {
          subtypes: [dog]
          body: !record { fields: [
            !record_field { name: pet_type  type: text }
            !record_field { name: name      type: text }
          ]  extension: ABSTRACT  discriminators: [pet_type] }
        }

        dog => !type_definition {
          supertypes: [pet]
          body: !record { supertypes: [pet]  fields: [
            !record_field { name: pet_type  type: text  optional: true  role: FIXED  value: "dog" }
            !record_field { name: name      type: text }
          ] }
        }

        shape => !type_definition {
          body: !record { fields: [
            !record_field { name: area  type: int32 }
          ]  extension: ABSTRACT }
        }

        reading => !type_definition {
          body: !record { fields: [
            !record_field { name: sensor  type: text }
          ]  extension: FINAL }
        }

        plain => !type_definition {
          body: !record { fields: [
            !record_field { name: note  type: text }
          ] }
        }
      }
      """
  }
}
